      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">0</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mechanisms to foster sustainable financing of local forest-based enterprises promoted for enhancing capacity of forest communities to be aware of carbon market opportunities to participate in carbon readiness activities.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This component will address capacity barrier 5 by increasing livelihood opportunities for communities through promoting climate-friendly income-generating activities and access to finance. Output 4.1 will provide for two financing models funded to support youth and women owned forest-based enterprise (Village Savings Loan Association and Growth Accelerator).</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2026-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1. Number of climate resilient livelihood initiatives implemented in target communities and percent of increase in income.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This outcome will address capacity barriers 1 and 5 by promoting sustainable alternatives for wood, charcoal and bush meat, and increasing livelihood opportunities for communities through promoting climate-friendly income-generating activities and promoting sustainable forest management activities linked to CCA and other communities. Under Output 3.1 the project will set up an agroforestry scheme (forest friendly cocoa, other crops) in at least 20 target communities with approximately 500 household beneficiaries from 500 ha at 1ha per household). 
Cocoa agroforestry scheme proposed for this project provides for a production system that incorporate development of cocoa and non-cocoa tree species (indigenous forest species) on the same plot along with fruit trees and vegetables. This design is intended to enhance the potential to achieve a range of benefits to the environment, climate, cocoa production, and socio-economic systems which may address deforestation, farmers&#x2019; livelihoods, and forest restoration.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2026-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="5000"></target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1: Percent increase in revenue for forest-based processed products</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This outcome will address capacity barriers 1, 2 and 3 through: Output 2.1. system developed to support community-based reduced impact logging in Commercial zones of community forests (mapping, inventory, environmental assessment, operational plan etc). Output 2.2. Output 2.2. A pilot reduced impact commercial timber extraction based on agreed national guidelines in at least one CF (Sokpo/ Konigar-B within the Northwest Forest landscape. This initiative will utilize a tool developed by USAID in 2016 &#x201c;Best Practices for Community-Based Low Impact Timber Harvesting in Liberia&#x201d; as well as leverage on the experience of the Ekuri Community in Nigeria, which won the UNDP&apos;s &#x201c;Equator Award&#x201d; in 2004 in recognition of the community&#x2019;s successes in reducing poverty through conservation and sustainable forest management.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
